Demand for highly sensitive particle and photon detection is supporting the use of microchannel plates (MCPs) across defense imaging, scientific instrumentation, aerospace research and specialized photonics systems. These components amplify very weak incoming signals, allowing detection systems to measure events that conventional sensors may struggle to resolve with the required sensitivity or timing.

